  "title": "Fed-GRPO: Reward-Signal-Driven Federated Group Relative Policy Optimization",
  "summary": "Fed-GRPO addresses privacy and data-sharing constraints in federated learning by enabling collaborative reasoning training without centralized data, leveraging reward signals generated during GRPO training to guide aggregation, local training, and communication. It achieves state-of-the-art performance on mathematical reasoning tasks while reducing communication by 32×.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Fed-GRPO uses signal-weighted aggregation to prioritize clients with stronger learning signals.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Fed-GRPO reduces communication by 32× while maintaining performance.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Fed-GRPO supports up to 621× compression under tight bandwidth budgets.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Extensive experiments on mathematical reasoning tasks show it outperforms FedAvg and approaches centralized training performance.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
